kind (Kubernetes IN Docker)
Copyright 2018 The Kubernetes Authors
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kind

  build/Containerfile is derived from kind's images/base/Dockerfile and has been
  modified.

  What comes from kind is the configuration that makes systemd run as PID 1 in a
  container: masking the units that cannot work there, pruning the *.wants
  directories, `ENV container=docker`, `STOPSIGNAL SIGRTMIN+3` and the reason
  for it, and the shape of the package grouping.

  What differs is the distribution (Fedora rather than Debian), the container
  runtime (CRI-O and crun rather than containerd), the cluster networking
  (Antrea), rootless operation under Podman quadlets, and everything kinc adds
  on top.

